    "prompt": "25 Explanation: The five rights of medication administration are a set of principles that guide the safe and accurate administration of medications to clients. They are designed to prevent medication errors and adverse drug reactions. The five rights are: right client (verify the identity of the client), right drug (check the label and the order of the medication), right dose (calculate and measure the correct amount of the medication), right route (select and prepare the appropriate route of administration), and right time (give the medication at the prescribed time or within an acceptable time frame). 89. What is informed consent? A legal document that gives permission for a medical procedure or treatment",
